cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite the preferred report citation below when referring to this
  research concept. This repository documents a proposed design and its
  evidence limits; it does not provide a validated instrument or software implementation.
title: "Pose-Resolved EM Scanner / Rover: Research Concept and Technical Audit"
authors:
  - family-names: Dik
    given-names: Philipp
version: "2026.09.25"
date-released: "2026-09-25"
url: "https://github.com/PhilDik/pose-resolved-em-scanner"
abstract: >-
  Research concept for joint interpretation of electromagnetic induction
  measurements using calibrated transmitter and receiver poses. The proposed
  embodiment uses one large transmitter loop and three separately read receiver
  coils on a common rotating carrier. Repeated registered measurements update
  the scene map while any pretrained model remains fixed. The documentation
  reviews prior art, supporting experiments, identifiability limits and future
  validation needs. Overall novelty and a measured performance advantage have
  not been established.
keywords:
  - electromagnetic induction
  - pose-resolved measurements
  - inverse problems
  - research concept
